From 340f8d69833e7dad7df672759a08a651cda111ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:15:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Kanban restart resume: an over-headroom prior
 session resumes, then compacts before the first model call

The planner used to refuse a resume at >= 85% of the compaction threshold (over_compaction_threshold),
so the run restarted from a 16k-char tail (hub ev 380043: 222,858 tok vs 231,200, 23.7 run-min lost).
Now admission copies the transcript as usual and marks restart_resume compaction: 'pending'; the worker
runs the agent's own _compress_context (trigger turn_start_threshold) before its first model call and
appends a second restart_resume event: compacted: true (+ compacted_messages/tokens), or fallback
compaction_failed / compaction_unavailable, after which the copied rows are soft-archived
(archive_and_compact with nothing to insert, on both SessionDB and the worker store) and the run starts
from today's transcript-tail context.
---
